From: =?UTF-8?q?=E9=A1=BA=E5=87=AF?= <daishun.ds@antgroup.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:18:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add openai-oauth backend (ChatGPT subscription via
 Codex OAuth)

Run graphify extraction on a ChatGPT Plus/Pro subscription instead of
pay-as-you-go API credit. Subscription OAuth tokens only authenticate
against the Codex Responses backend (chatgpt.com/backend-api/codex/responses,
SSE), not api.openai.com, so this adds a dedicated stdlib-only client:
device-code login (python -m graphify.openai_oauth), isolated credential
store (~/.graphify/openai-oauth.json, created 0600, fsynced atomic
pid-unique writes), lock-guarded single-flight refresh with backoff and
cross-process rotation adoption, JWT chatgpt_account_id extraction, and
429/5xx/network backoff (incl. mid-stream IncompleteRead). Custom
User-Agent on every request (Cloudflare 530s Python-urllib's). Handles
the terminal response.incomplete event; timeouts stay typed as
TimeoutError; token values never leak into errors.

Covers extract/update semantic extraction (image files become text notes),
the plain-text path (label), and dedup-llm (credential counts as configured
key). Default model gpt-6-luna, reasoning effort medium. Serial by default
like claude-cli; GRAPHIFY_OPENAI_OAUTH_PARALLEL=1 opts in. Never
auto-detected; select with --backend openai-oauth. Zero new deps.
